course: dictionary
lesson: 4591
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word herb is one of them. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means. A herb is a plant used to flavour food, to make medicine or tea, or, in science, any small plant with a soft stem.
explain: «Fresh herbs» and «herb garden» are about cooking and growing. The clues are fresh, garden and food, so a herb here is a plant you can add to a meal. «Herbal tea» tells you the plant is used to make a drink.
explain: In science, a herb is not about flavour at all. It means a plant with a soft stem, not a woody one like a tree or bush. Banana plants look like trees, but they are giant herbs. Their «trunk» is made of tightly rolled leaves, not wood.
fact: A herb is a plant used for flavour, medicine or tea.
fact: Basil, mint, parsley, rosemary and thyme are common herbs.
fact: A «herb garden» is a garden where herbs are grown.
fact: In science, a herb is any small plant with a soft stem, not woody like a tree.
fact: Banana plants are giant herbs, not trees.
fact: Long ago, people used herbs as medicine, but many of these remedies did not work.
exercise: Mum cut some «fresh herbs» from the windowsill and sprinkled them on the soup. What are herbs here? | Wooden benches with high backs | Tools for cutting bread | Small stones from the garden | *Plants whose leaves add flavour to food
exercise: In science, a herb is a plant with a soft stem. Which of these is a herb in science? | *A small plant with a soft stem | A rose bush | An oak tree | A pine tree
exercise: Ella reads about a «herb garden» in a gardening book. What does herb garden mean? | A garden for swimming | *A garden where herbs are grown | A garden for shoes | A garden full of trees
test: Banana plants look like trees, but they are giant herbs. Why are they herbs? | Because they have proper seeds | Because they grow underground | *Because they are not woody, and their trunks are made of rolled leaves | Because they grow in shops
test: Dad makes «herbal tea» from chamomile. What does herbal tea mean? | *A drink made from a plant used for flavour or medicine | Tea served cold in summer | Tea with lots of sugar | Water with no taste at all
exam: Which best describes a herb? | *A plant used for flavour, medicine or tea, often with a soft stem | A large tree with a woody trunk | A stone found on the beach | A wooden bench with a high back
